schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Cryptocurrency, Blockchain, and Decentralisation
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    Money that exists only as digital records, moved directly between
    people via a shared, tamper-resistant ledger (blockchain) copied across
    many computers, with no single bank, company, or government running the
    system (decentralisation).
  source_traditions:
    - Bitcoin (2009), the first cryptocurrency, as the article's origin point
    - mutual-credit / community-currency traditions (the article's explicit "digital version of mutual credit" framing for the Sarafu Network)
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Used as the plain-language on-ramp article for readers with no prior
    crypto exposure, translating blockchain/decentralisation into a
    "shared lending notebook" analogy drawn from seed-library practice.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - a coin (native money of its own chain, e.g. Bitcoin, ether) vs a token (built atop an existing chain for a specific purpose)
    - proof of work vs proof of stake as different ways a blockchain achieves that shared, tamper-resistant record
  important_distinctions:
    - owning cryptocurrency means owning a key that moves a record, not owning a physical thing (the article's core reframing)
    - community-set rules (what a token represents) vs blockchain-provided honesty (the ledger just keeps the count straight)
  tensions:
    - the article's own honest framing (you almost certainly don't need crypto) vs four specific cases where it is presented as genuinely useful
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Framing decentralisation via the "farmers' market without a central
    boss" analogy risks understating the real infrastructure, expertise,
    and governance that blockchains still require (node operators,
    protocol developers, validator/miner economics) — the article
    simplifies for a first-time audience rather than engaging this.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/what-is-cryptocurrency.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  source_lineage: what-is-cryptocurrency.md
